        "id": 1966830
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-28T21:00:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi William and Thomas, this is a feature we need to rollout LL privacy in ChromeOS, which is already fully enabled in android. So I think this sysprop is not useful to android in practice. But it is a feature that android currently doesn\u0027t support. I am open to use ifdef.",
      "parentUuid": "44db024c_be775bb7",
      "revId": "bb44623eaf6bfff0727e62f0a4f4ae56dc80912b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9964b64b_4a225fad",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1966830
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-28T21:02:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Using a flag just because I am open to also test it in android, and I would like to manage it like other features.",
      "parentUuid": "f8972986_6985b044",
      "revId": "bb44623eaf6bfff0727e62f0a4f4ae56dc80912b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "95a82394_befe18da",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1904823
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-28T21:03:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why not rolling it out for Android as well? CC @rwt@google.com",
      "parentUuid": "9964b64b_4a225fad",
      "revId": "bb44623eaf6bfff0727e62f0a4f4ae56dc80912b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "884b4e31_4682257b",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1966830
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-28T22:35:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is mainly because at least for the Android phone, the privacy mode is by default enabled. As a result, the host address is always resolvable random. I don\u0027t see a use case when the android needs to run with a public address + privacy mode, or non-privacy mode + a random address. But for Chrome OS, we currently have non-privacy mode + public address, so we need a transition state to fully migrate to the same as android.",
      "parentUuid": "95a82394_befe18da",
      "revId": "bb44623eaf6bfff0727e62f0a4f4ae56dc80912b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c1545d4e_f23aa454",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1966830
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-28T22:41:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For Chrome OS, the user will transit from non-privacy mode + public address to privacy mode + public address. Then if the user wants to get full privacy, the user will disconnect LE devices, then reboot to enable privacy mode + random address. Then manually re-pair the LE devices. This is not needed for android.",
      "parentUuid": "884b4e31_4682257b",
      "revId": "bb44623eaf6bfff0727e62f0a4f4ae56dc80912b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3a98fcec_43844dc5",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1904823
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-29T00:16:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Even if there isn\u0027t any usecase for it, I think this is fine to have the feature on the Android codebase if it doesn\u0027t affect phones which aren\u0027t using it. Will let @rwt@google.com chime in here.",
      "parentUuid": "c1545d4e_f23aa454",
      "revId": "bb44623eaf6bfff0727e62f0a4f4ae56dc80912b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "99ee6d4d_d390081a",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882530
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-29T16:39:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Android doesn\u0027t need this feature. I don\u0027t have any problem as long as it is clear that these are Floss specific, and don\u0027t confuse future readers.",
      "parentUuid": "3a98fcec_43844dc5",
      "revId": "bb44623eaf6bfff0727e62f0a4f4ae56dc80912b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bd946c11_45cc72fc",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1904823
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-30T00:03:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Updating my view on this: Android Bluetooth stack \u003d Android + ChromeOS right now. So any feature that is needed for ChromeOS should be added to the stack and rolled out using a flag (without any ifdef). If the feature is only used by ChromeOS, it should indeed be documented in the code and our QA team will verify that the feature doesn\u0027t add any regression. So I\u0027m fine here as well.",
      "parentUuid": "99ee6d4d_d390081a",
      "revId": "bb44623eaf6bfff0727e62f0a4f4ae56dc80912b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
